meta {
  name: A mark you cannot reach is missing, not forbidden
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/periods/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 404
}

docs {
  404, NEVER 403, and the same for a mark that exists but lies outside the
  caller's reach. 403 on a real row would confirm that a pupil was marked in a
  class the caller is not entitled to know about, and attendance is exactly
  the kind of record where that inference is worth something - it says who was
  in the building.

  The bulk register is the one exception in this folder, and only because it
  has to be: a teacher sending forty pupils gets a 422 listing the ones out of
  reach, because failing the whole register with no explanation would be
  unusable. It names pupils the caller already named.
}
